{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7d9ee08351c261685ebba2c661785002e0cd02f83d7866dc34edaa1545d5e8c0","digest":{"component_or_area":"local-dev-env documentation","key_entities":["docs/local-dev-env.md","tests/conftest.py::pytest_sessionfinish","tests/conftest.py::_no_repo_root_leaks","tests/conftest.py::_no_repo_commits","git status --porcelain","REPO ISOLATION FAILURE"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","test guard","session isolation","git state","concurrent modification"],"propositions":["The local-dev-env documentation omits the session-level working-tree backstop guard from its misfire list.","The pytest_sessionfinish working-tree backstop detects concurrent modifications (commits, rebases, branch switches, editor saves) via porcelain diff across the whole session.","The session backstop reports a single REPO ISOLATION FAILURE at session end rather than blaming an individual straddling test like the two per-test guards do.","Documentation must clarify that the session backstop fires once at session tail, distinguishing it from the per-test guards that fire during teardown."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787869124539866001,"uuid":"0c29ac0c-81ca-4e7a-93de-e724a880a645"}